## AMD GPU Drivers

AMD Instinct GPUs use the `amdgpu` kernel driver included in the
{{ distro_name }} kernel, so no additional kernel module is needed. The compute
image does need the GPU firmware (part of `linux-firmware`, from the
distribution's BaseOS repository); without it, `amdgpu` cannot initialize the
GPUs. The
ROCm runtime and tools come from AMD's ROCm repository for
EL{{ distro_version }}: the HIP runtime on the compute nodes, and the HIP
development tools on the head node for building applications. `${rocm_repo}`
names the repository, and with it the ROCm release (a `main` directory under
<https://repo.radeon.com/rocm/rhel{{ distro_version }}/>). AMD's HIP runtime
package requires the ROCm compiler toolchain, so the compute image also gains
it; together these packages add about 2.3 GB to the image.

The distribution's udev rules give all users access to the GPU devices
(`/dev/kfd` and `/dev/dri/renderD*`), so users need no additional group
membership to run GPU jobs.

<!-- ohpc_begin -->
<!-- ohpc_if_set enable_amd_gpu_driver -->
```bash
# Add the ROCm repository to the head node
rpm --import https://repo.radeon.com/rocm/rocm.gpg.key
{{ pkg_add_repo }} "${rocm_repo}"

# Add the ROCm repository to the compute nodes
{{ compute_run("rpm --import https://repo.radeon.com/rocm/rocm.gpg.key") }}
{{ compute_run("dnf -y config-manager --add-repo ${rocm_repo}") }}

# Install the GPU firmware and the ROCm runtime on the compute nodes
{{ compute_install(["linux-firmware", "rocm-hip-runtime"]) }}
{{ compute_install(["rocminfo", "rocm-smi-lib"]) }}

# Install the ROCm HIP development tools on the head node
{{ head_install(["rocm-hip-runtime-devel", "hipcc", "rocminfo"]) }}
```
<!-- ohpc_fi -->
<!-- ohpc_end -->

::: {.tip}
**Tip:** Once the compute nodes boot, `rocminfo` on a compute node lists each
GPU as an agent (e.g. `gfx908` for an Instinct MI100), and `rocm-smi` shows
their temperature, power and utilization. AMD supports ROCm with its own
`amdgpu-dkms` kernel module rather than the in-kernel driver; if a GPU does not
appear, install `amdgpu-dkms` from the same repository's `amdgpu` channel in the
compute image.

When the head node has no GPU, `hipcc` cannot detect the target and builds for
a default architecture that may not run on the compute nodes' GPUs. Name the
GPU architecture explicitly, e.g. `hipcc --offload-arch=gfx908 -o app app.hip`
for an Instinct MI100.
:::
